==Free-to-play Strategy==
{{Otheruses|def=no|strategies for [[members]]|Slayer task/Greater demons}}
The only place [[free-to-play]] players can kill greater demons is in the [[Demonic Ruins]]. This location is notable because players will have [[prayer points]] automatically restored while standing in the area. However, it is also in a [[multicombat area]] in high-level [[Wilderness]], meaning '''there is a high risk of getting killed by [[Player killing|other players]]'''. When killing greater demons here, players should bring as few items as possible to minimize risk.

Level 43 [[Prayer]] is recommended to use [[Protect from Melee]], as it will negate all damage from the demons. The Ruins' prayer restoring effect allows players to use Protect from Melee constantly without needing to restore prayer points at an [[altar]]. Because all damage is negated by prayer, defensive [[armour]] is unnecessary and players can prioritize items with [[strength bonus]]es to maximise damage ouptput. By bringing a good [[weapon]] (i.e. a [[rune scimitar]] or [[Silverlight]]), an [[amulet of strength]] or [[amulet of power]], and a [[Mooleta]], players can maximise damage while minimizing the risk of losing items to other players.

Alternatively, players can prioritize items with a [[Prayer items|prayer bonus]] to allow use of combat boosting prayers such as [[Superhuman Strength]] or [[Improved Reflexes]]. By bringing a good weapon (the [[rune mace]] notably has a +4 prayer bonus), a [[monk's robe top]], a [[monk's robe bottom]], and a [[holy symbol]], prayer points will drain slowly enough to allow players to use at least one of these prayers in combination with Protect from Melee for a 10% [[Strength]] or accuracy boost.

Players without Level 43 Prayer can alternatively use one of the multiple safespots at the Demonic Ruins to use [[Ranged]] or [[Magic]] attacks to kill the greater demons, though this is generally not recommended due to the risk of losing [[runes]] or [[ammo]] to other players.
